d-2}} | $\\frac{37}{3}$ | $\\frac{221}{12}$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=\\frac{t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 t}{3} + 2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=\\frac{(2)^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 (2)}{3} + 2=(2)+\\left(- \\frac{8}{3}\\right)+(1)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $$\n\\displaystyle y=\\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{2 t}{3} + 3.\n$$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(3)=\\frac{3 (3)^{2}}{4} - \\frac{2 (3)}{3} + 3=(3)+(-2)+\\left(\\frac{27}{4}\\right)=\\frac{31}{4}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $x=\\frac{t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 t}{3} + 2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(4)=\\frac{(4)^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 (4)}{3} + 2=(2)+\\left(- \\frac{16}{3}\\right)+(4)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $\\frac{11}{12}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{19}{12}$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $\\frac{37}{12}$ | $\\frac{14}{3}$ | $\\frac{31}{4}$ | $\\frac{37}{3}$ | $\\frac{221}{12}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ac25246-3153-5bc7-9c7a-e1323ff4efcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697637}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697637} :answer-field/id #uuid "29dd3737-7889-5d0d-aee8-9285c4931e86" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79a8f1f-cb00-506d-bd4b-a3fb8ef0e424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697650}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697650} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b9ac73b-7b7d-5e34-bbe8-45b0c4d75776" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac8f7f0-05b6-55ff-a51f-14433d0c00a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697648}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697648} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a1377a-b174-5967-b4e3-0492fec907ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "68ea139d-8f83-5ecb-b070-c337ebdf0983" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2t-1,\\qquad y=t^2+1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks. Use the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, the first entry in the $x$-row is $x(-2)=2(-2)-1=-5$.\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-5$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $y$ | {{field-3}} | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The row tells us which formula to use, and the column tells us the value of $t$.\n\nFor the $x$-entry under $t=-1$, substitute $-1$ into $x=2t-1$:\n\n$$\nx(-1)=2(-1)-1=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nFor the $x$-entry under $t=2$, use the same formula:\n\n$$\nx(2)=2(2)-1=4-1=3.\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-entry under $t=-2$, use $y=t^2+1$. Square the entire negative number:\n\n$$\ny(-2)=(-2)^2+1=4+1=5.\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa20801-08a2-5e2d-950e-e3cc94ff6da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697633} {:answer/id #uuid "33dd7ec4-0126-5adf-812f-11166227af2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697639} {:answer/id #uuid "4612bcf9-ddbe-577d-8ecf-f5c64ae4b720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697640} {:answer/id #uuid "620e6851-0bd2-5bf8-b300-14d8ebc4ddda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697641} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe19e41-701e-5fe0-b25b-dd12d35b61a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697647}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697639} :answer-field/id #uuid "b429b33e-f0af-50a0-b280-3a1a49ca466d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "86dd7dd4-5849-554c-9e2d-91445aacb13c" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right),\\qquad y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right),\\qquad -3\\le t\\le 4,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values. Angles are in radians.\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $b$ | $1$ | $c$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nFind the exact value of $a-b+c$." :question/worked-solution "Read each letter's row and column before substituting.\n\nThe entry $a$ is an $x$-value at $t=-3$:\n\n$$\na=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi(-3)}{4}\\right)=\\sin\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHere $\\sin(-\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta$ and $\\sin(3\\pi/4)=\\sqrt{2}/2$.\n\nThe entry $b$ is a $y$-value at $t=-2$:\n\n$$\nb=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(-2)}{6}\\right)=\\cos\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nCosine is even, so $\\cos(-\\pi/3)=\\cos(\\pi/3)$.\n\nThe entry $c$ is a $y$-value at $t=1$:\n\n$$\nc=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(1)}{6}\\right)=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substitute these three entries into the requested expression, keeping the subtraction before $b$:\n\n$$\na-b+c=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3f6cd6f-feb8-5fe8-8a90-33632f5509a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697651}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697651} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d405c02-fc58-51d3-b300-ae1c90f40fc4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1160877a-343d-5fc8-aac7-64b1af59bba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697635} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a46afb-ed30-514f-a742-c43b99568561" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bcf4e3f-6edb-5253-90d7-a2b123cbc029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697646}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697646} :answer-field/id #uuid "80b84a21-8b7e-5c23-91e4-90c00658f335" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fca75a6f-ed74-5c52-b7db-81a5147488d0" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=t^2-t,\\qquad y=\\frac{t+1}{t-1},\\qquad -3\\le t\\le 0.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $12$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "The missing $x$-entry is in the column $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=t^2-t$:\n\n$$\nx(-2)=(-2)^2-(-2)=4+2=6.\n$$\n\nFor the missing $y$-entries, substitute the column's parameter into both the numerator and the denominator of $y=\\frac{t+1}{t-1}$:\n\n$$\ny(-3)=\\frac{-3+1}{-3-1}=\\frac{-2}{-4}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\n$$\ny(0)=\\frac{0+1}{0-1}=\\frac{1}{-1}=-1.\n$$\n\nThe denominators are nonzero at all the listed parameter values. The completed table is\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $12$ | $6$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $0$ | $-1$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec46b73-c5f6-5155-959c-ca6e0c3d1663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/60/60a8e096bb5a75c2b9d719cb7e8cae14fb27bc9d8e4b33455bc562c731382d9e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697895} {:answer/id #uuid "865b8979-1018-585a-94ed-051c773c0096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/12/12ced3191f8d54a6d579de66db1a0f291de774a6365f0a047269b2d822b67223.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697899} {:answer/id #uuid "92bce595-3de9-5315-a86a-f69867d20547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1b/1b6df959601589325952b589fdd198e5655b827a0fade7d27968e8295855ff6b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697900} {:answer/id #uuid "c772bb43-715e-5648-baeb-0e6e47a14099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0e/0e57de3a6543dce1df686135dc40e855e7487f5eb15f48aa63da28bcd5cdb094.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697904} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5aa83a-8c1f-58c1-b2c8-ee3307ba8194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4d/4d70fcd150196f121250a2f3bf1460adb87e4f91e51f838807814de9edcff54e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697906}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697906} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0f6b3cb-b6b7-5010-be72-77857f2bad2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3bd93405-82bc-5458-ab8c-fc0a7f96a9e3" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t(t-2),\\qquad y=t(t+2),\\qquad -2\\leq t\\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Create a table of paired coordinates. First calculate the $x$-values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $8$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow calculate the $y$-values at the same parameter values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $8$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n\nThe successive points are $(8,0)$, $(3,-1)$, $(0,0)$, $(-1,3)$ and $(0,8)$. Both coordinates turn within the interval: $x=(t-1)^2-1$ has minimum $-1$ at $t=1$, while $y=(t+1)^2-1$ has minimum $-1$ at $t=-1$. Plot a smooth curve through the paired points in parameter order. It dips below the $x$-axis through $(3,-1)$, passes through the origin, then bends left of the $y$-axis through $(-1,3)$ before reaching $(0,8)$. All five choices share the endpoints and the origin, so those three checkpoints alone cannot decide the answer. Check both interior bends.\n\n![The curve through the calculated points](images/86/8644be497d26e662b3b867539ee7b8d0dd812fac915e55db7b05045592a4fc6e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171dba7b-75a8-5827-b2b7-f3f105018aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f0/f07139da8afc6442b5d9281b35a6fd87c1cbcd3cd1e5a692afd45cf7a06e5a1a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697889} {:answer/id #uuid "1b08777a-5263-568c-8e9a-927145630fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/78/783773aee472c70476a015a44fb648a8e59ac81bb8b564e2de6fede2a3c7cec8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697890} {:answer/id #uuid "3a872233-4f07-505d-b731-f999cd3d4b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/33/331b287274e591bba469912c94bb7a7b6901dc929184d9c352ce88d8ca89a4ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697892} {:answer/id #uuid "f237f7bb-1ab1-5d28-8739-08cf56324c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/dc/dca67dd9991b9a24320fcc8527020926b9c14400f82c26d86657d4f76fc6436f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697907} {:answer/id #uuid "f77a222c-1429-5aa3-ba95-e1aa7abf488b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/7b/7bb54e148382c9b93b3669893a0f9672dcd442acd6db2ebed4c5b5a3c8ac42f5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697908}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697892} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e236298-acd4-58ed-84ad-c655d28e371f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "596432d1-4b77-548d-b59e-39a7ad303e6d" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t+2,\\qquad y=1-t,\\qquad -2\\leq t\\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Create a table of paired coordinates. First calculate the $x$-values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow calculate the $y$-values at the same parameter values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe paired coordinates are $(0,3)$, $(1,2)$, $(2,1)$, $(3,0)$ and $(4,-1)$. They lie on a decreasing straight line. Keep only the segment from $(0,3)$ to $(4,-1)$, with both endpoints included. A line with the right slope but different endpoints is not the required graph.\n\n![The curve through the calculated points](images/82/8227fb9f808f8b7622b2d3910efa11ce6d87b8085b4d7e24a77a342306532ee4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf915d8-6386-5c54-be79-20a4aeaf541b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/62/627e47bf56eb39ef2d2c76dbdc0025fe931e7dccc9a672aff34a81f10cb51ec6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697891} {:answer/id #uuid "70f0a849-b7ae-5bf7-b634-34370e5ae990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/02/02ee60db4d6765efaf9bde2e139017c67541afb341b144b47deb9d8e9a159e9a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697896} {:answer/id #uuid "93455f0c-22b5-5c6e-bce7-25a8d0d6293c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f9/f91bcece50a80cfd66cc9608a93072cd7089025b37ed09055ec7720538d037fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697901} {:answer/id #uuid "9591fb7f-d240-540e-b68b-21991e37a93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d3/d369859178cc839d6f4299e44e79f80f5d8e3341a82cab4a317b8265aa75dddd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697902} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3af7bb-aeeb-504c-8499-dc8dbb741f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/87/87c5054212819dd11c81cb4efb4e892274d1ca290cf96547d0c287531c469f45.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697903}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697902} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e6e7cbc-d38a-5510-9dc3-2ff6464a025d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7644270e-57aa-5c69-8e0b-cd91ed7f2919" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t^2-1,\\qquad y=2-t,\\qquad -1\\leq t\\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Create a table of paired coordinates. First calculate the $x$-values:\n\n| $t$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow calculate the $y$-values at the same parameter values:\n\n| $t$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nThe points are $(0,3)$, $(-1,2)$, $(0,1)$ and $(3,0)$. As $t$ runs from $-1$ to $0$, $x$ decreases to $-1$; as $t$ runs from $0$ to $2$, $x$ increases to $3$. Meanwhile $y$ decreases throughout. Plot the smooth right-opening arc through these points. Its leftmost point is $(-1,2)$, and its included endpoints are $(0,3)$ and $(3,0)$. The two arms have different lengths because the parameter interval is asymmetric.\n\n![The curve through the calculated points](images/93/9346e80ef10f528dd956f6d11b511b106e39c9d2724a6be0c6e60f9e73afe183.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "$x=-3$ requires $t=0$ or $t=-2$, both excluded. The lower bound on $x$ is strict." :answer/id #uuid "02bf8594-fd10-51bb-899f-6f0738f7db21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697909} {:answer/feedback "The lower bound on $x$ is approached at the excluded boundary, while the upper bound on $y$ is attained inside the domain." :answer/id #uuid "066c6421-e8cb-5f6b-834c-952f021293a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697910} {:answer/feedback "The vertex for $x$ is at $t=-1$, outside the allowed domain. For $t>0$, the sharper bound is $x>-3$." :answer/id #uuid "3e2acba4-386f-5964-9c3f-826c2e75ee46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -4,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697914} {:answer/feedback "The value $y=4$ occurs at the allowed parameter $t=2$; a strict parameter bound does not exclude an interior maximum." :answer/id #uuid "786dddd9-115e-5687-845d-cc23f3c97bf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697917} {:answer/feedback "The expression $4-(t-2)^2$ is at most $4$, not at least $4$." :answer/id #uuid "e1b9c4cf-22a1-58fe-af03-812c0a4d587d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697927}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697910} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d82b3f-04f3-5b41-8f57-443a382e0133" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "468940dc-fef5-52fb-97ca-09170efe4223" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2+2t-3,\\quad y=4t-t^2,\\quad t>0,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Complete the square for each coordinate, keeping the restriction $t>0$ throughout.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=t^2+2t-3 \\\\\n  &=(t+1)^2-4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unrestricted minimum $-4$ would require $t=-1$, which is not allowed. In the given domain, $t+1>1$, so $(t+1)^2>1$ and $x>-3$. The boundary value $-3$ would require $t=0$ or $t=-2$, neither of which is allowed. Every value $x>-3$ is attained by $t=-1+\\sqrt{x+4}>0$. Thus the range of $x$ is $x>-3$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=4t-t^2 \\\\\n  &=-(t-2)^2+4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence $y\\le 4$. The maximum $4$ is attained at $t=2$, which is allowed even though the parameter inequality is strict. Every value $y\\le 4$ is attained by $t=2+\\sqrt{4-y}>0$, so there is no lower bound.\n\nTherefore, the coordinate ranges are $x>-3$ and $y\\le 4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Subtracting the nonnegative quantity $t^2$ from $3$ gives an upper bound on $y$." :answer/id #uuid "160f02aa-e38a-53a2-808d-576d50bd0de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697911} {:answer/feedback "The minimum of $x$ is $-3$ at $t=2$, and the maximum of $y$ is $3$ at $t=0$." :answer/id #uuid "7369e6dd-083c-57ce-9a37-8a6f4f63ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697916} {:answer/feedback "The nonnegative square in $x=(t-2)^2-3$ gives a lower bound on $x$." :answer/id #uuid "cc8fccc4-9896-534b-9da8-76559ee0736c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697922} {:answer/feedback "Both extremizing parameter values are allowed, so both equalities are included." :answer/id #uuid "d71b3e40-f663-5d75-a8f1-284afa23e1a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697925} {:answer/feedback "The constant term is not the minimum of this quadratic. Complete the square to find $(t-2)^2-3$." :answer/id #uuid "f5c05357-8df0-509d-849d-c875c630afab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 1,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697928}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697916} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cebc80-4738-5ebe-8c01-c1b3c2fc2e72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "921cecba-5183-5dd0-9ca3-7a72a38cdb3c" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2-4t+1,\\quad y=3-t^2,\\quad t\\in(-\\infty,\\infty),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$, complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=t^2-4t+1 \\\\\n  &=(t^2-4t+4)-3 \\\\\n  &=(t-2)^2-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square takes every nonnegative value as $t$ ranges over all real numbers. Thus $x\\ge -3$, with equality at $t=2$, and there is no upper bound.\n\nFor $y$, the fact that $t^2\\ge 0$ gives $y=3-t^2\\le 3$. Equality occurs at $t=0$, and $y$ takes every value below $3$.\n\nTherefore, the coordinate ranges are $x\\ge -3$ and $y\\le 3$. These bounds need not occur at the same parameter value; they describe the two coordinate ranges separately."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Multiplication by $-2$ reverses the inequality, so $x$ decreases as $t$ increases." :answer/id #uuid "1969ae88-530d-5474-9986-2a5824242faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697912} {:answer/feedback "$x=2$ occurs at $t=1$, and every smaller value is attained." :answer/id #uuid "31cb0908-dcc1-50f1-b369-f048bc05f69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697913} {:answer/feedback "$t=0$ is outside the parameter domain; the largest allowed value of $x$ occurs at $t=1$." :answer/id #uuid "b22be577-bd88-50e0-9525-13a148521ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697920} {:answer/feedback "The allowed parameter $t=1$ gives $x=2$, so equality must be included." :answer/id #uuid "cbaff8af-eaa9-5d07-a0ea-eb49afaf4a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697921} {:answer/feedback "$2$ is the maximum, but larger values of $t$ produce every smaller value of $x$." :answer/id #uuid "d1131d1a-0885-54dc-a155-ec41f37b9437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697923}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697913} :answer-field/id #uuid "a96a175d-4d83-5b26-a9cf-ae9c9434eb35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d8fe94e2-a021-5fc4-a910-6c60b0f92f91" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4-2t,\\quad y=t^2+1,\\quad t\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x$?" :question/worked-solution "Since $t\\ge 1$, multiplying by $-2$ reverses the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt &\\ge 1 \\\\\n-2t &\\le -2 \\\\\n4-2t &\\le 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=2$ is attained at $t=1$. As $t$ increases without bound, $x$ decreases without bound. Every value below $2$ occurs: for any $x\\le 2$, the parameter $t=(4-x)/2$ satisfies $t\\ge 1$.\n\nTherefore, the range is $x\\le 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6884502-f500-5d93-bf3f-92ae0c495ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698080}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698080} :answer-field/id #uuid "06473d97-a7d7-564d-aa7e-8763299388ab" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "741fe4c2-7dd8-5052-ba30-2f2546e42bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698066}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698066} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c4deb16-fcd5-54f2-9380-351c84810d90" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0f01368-92f3-5d0a-a665-174604ef2bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698081}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698081} :answer-field/id #uuid "52738c9c-b76d-5919-8300-ad1fe30e0c48" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b34baae2-ee3f-5def-874d-60d8f84ddcf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698075}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698075} :answer-field/id #uuid "86d017b5-5b42-58a9-b319-a4cf4afbb996" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2670d8be-0477-54cf-a518-8018afaf7db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698056}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698056} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e4bb5e-a9e7-54ee-b6a0-de5566f88ce5" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027ae5f1-6672-59fa-8f0f-307a2eb6acf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698052}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698052} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2083eb0-a087-5b94-b273-fcecd2480411" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "72d3f4c9-33bf-5f30-b80b-da478efa9772" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2-3\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=2\\sin\\theta-4,\\qquad 0\\le\\theta<2\\pi,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x\\le$ {{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}} $\\le y$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately. On $0\\le\\theta<2\\pi$, both sine and cosine attain every value from $-1$ to $1$.\n\nFor $x$, multiplying by $-3$ reverses the inequalities. Add $2$, then write the bounds in increasing order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta \\le 1 \\\\\n3 &\\ge -3\\cos\\theta \\ge -3 \\\\\n5 &\\ge 2-3\\cos\\theta \\ge -1 \\\\\n-1 &\\le x\\le 5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y$, multiply by $2$ and subtract $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta \\le 1 \\\\\n-2 &\\le 2\\sin\\theta \\le 2 \\\\\n-6 &\\le 2\\sin\\theta-4 \\le -2 \\\\\n-6 &\\le y\\le -2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth endpoints of each range are attained. Therefore, $-1\\le x\\le 5$ and $-6\\le y\\le -2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "332df4cf-1aa7-5def-ac81-18090e8754b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698059}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698059} :answer-field/id #uuid "1de877d1-e3e8-5f4d-9f56-8fe66484e09e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "421418e5-8044-5ed8-83be-e1f753eaa97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698060}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698060} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed68c0d-c744-54c2-9465-cac942949c37" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bb5b357-556a-5593-91ff-68eae0c62790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698063} :answer-field/id #uuid "94417408-44d9-5515-9187-e00e5d1d1e7a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "672234a8-c686-5cfa-81ef-cb5ab6360d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698064} :answer-field/id #uuid "b568fbde-dc32-5318-a730-67ed930ee6ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5985019-521b-5cf1-a91d-acd27c39e1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698077} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca456ea8-28ea-59dc-9b2a-3890cba95d01" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b20220b-c18f-5293-9b0a-959eb0e5216b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698062}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698062} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc171f86-7773-50ca-a5d5-38e36972745c" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8714e1c8-2824-5d74-a7c0-997378cd464d" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-2\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=3\\sin\\theta-1,\\qquad 0<\\theta\\le\\frac{3\\pi}{2},\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ as appropriate in each comparison blank.\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x\\le$ {{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}} $\\le y$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The parameter interval does not cover a full turn. Check the sine and cosine extrema within the interval, as well as the excluded and included endpoints.\n\nFor $x$, cosine reaches $-1$ at $\\theta=\\pi$. It approaches $1$ as $\\theta$ approaches $0$ from above, but never equals $1$ on the given interval. Thus $-1\\le\\cos\\theta<1$. Multiplying by $-2$ reverses the comparisons, including the strict one:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta <1 \\\\\n2 &\\ge -2\\cos\\theta >-2 \\\\\n3 &\\ge 1-2\\cos\\theta >-1 \\\\\n-1 &<x\\le 3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe upper bound $3$ occurs at $\\theta=\\pi$; the lower bound $-1$ is not attained.\n\nFor $y$, sine reaches $1$ at the interior point $\\theta=\\pi/2$ and $-1$ at the included endpoint $\\theta=3\\pi/2$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta \\le 1 \\\\\n-3 &\\le 3\\sin\\theta \\le 3 \\\\\n-4 &\\le 3\\sin\\theta-1 \\le 2 \\\\\n-4 &\\le y\\le 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe ranges are $-1<x\\le 3$ and $-4\\le y\\le 2$. Sine attains both extremes even though $\\theta=0$ is excluded. Continuity ensures that all values between the stated bounds occur. The coordinate ranges are considered separately; their extremes need not occur at the same parameter value."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eb9e4e9-9834-5dc1-a83a-29d6cc66c85a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le y\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698058} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb55ae9-9283-592a-a55c-f34216a124ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\quad -1\\le y\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698067} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5b6e1d-9658-59c8-b343-a5bc0a08a6ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6\\le x\\le 6,\\quad -10\\le y\\le 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698074} {:answer/id #uuid "be72512f-a3fe-5797-bf53-c018e08c0794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\le x\\le 3,\\quad -5\\le y\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698078} {:answer/id #uuid "e24f7af4-f995-5553-9cc0-f102ae3b4206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\le x\\le 5,\\quad -3\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698083}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698078} :answer-field/id #uuid "0420dcfb-cdde-55fd-bd1f-1a24131299f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "91f69afd-c235-591f-ab3c-fc8cc28f1ac7" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=5\\sin\\theta,\\qquad 0\\le\\theta<2\\pi,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately. On $0\\le\\theta<2\\pi$, both sine and cosine attain every value from $-1$ to $1$.\n\nFor $x$, multiply the cosine bounds by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta \\le 1 \\\\\n-3 &\\le 3\\cos\\theta \\le 3 \\\\\n-3 &\\le x \\le 3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y$, multiply the sine bounds by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta \\le 1 \\\\\n-5 &\\le 5\\sin\\theta \\le 5 \\\\\n-5 &\\le y \\le 5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the ranges are $-3\\le x\\le 3$ and $-5\\le y\\le 5$. All four bounds are attained within the parameter interval; excluding $2\\pi$ does not remove any coordinate bound."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95080386-ba52-5508-83c3-b56c1665d28b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698126}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698126} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaeba00c-d120-5e96-9059-a314382c774e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d9c76bd-b0e8-51bc-8963-f6991f6f5009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698127} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca74996f-a9e1-588f-822c-8a43fe4b66cb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "941c8040-96d6-5850-af56-8af967babfbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698125}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698125} :answer-field/id #uuid "d271a935-7a01-5a55-b8ee-31c44c8d02dd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6eb50d16-40b6-5dfc-b62f-e9e8d896c408" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 1,\\qquad y=- t^{2} - 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=- 2 \\left(-2\\right) - 1=3$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | {{field-2}} | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=- t^{2} - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=- \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 1 \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=- 2 t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=- 2 \\left(-1\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $y=- t^{2} - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) &=- \\left(2\\right)^{2} - 1 \\\\ &=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-5$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab3f1ae-28b2-5f8c-993e-34643d52a9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698114}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698114} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cb7f62-fc37-5436-ad36-35291c3bd9d5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3685ab30-02fd-52d8-8b72-935c9467a6e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698112}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698112} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1558c42-7ae1-57f5-ac82-b5bab4db30ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e575b9a-1adc-5e76-83bf-a687525b0013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698110}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698110} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb09eae-223f-5d30-9183-b5e9215b9107" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "714507d9-4ce5-52aa-b483-53ba86dda909" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=1 - t,\\qquad y=2 - t^{2},\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=1 - \\left(-2\\right)=3$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $1$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-1}} | $-2$ |" :question/worked-solution "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=1$. Substitute into $y=2 - t^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) &=2 - \\left(1\\right)^{2} \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=1 - t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=1 - \\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=2 - t^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=2 - \\left(0\\right)^{2} \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc8abf18-1dad-5023-998f-ee754e335050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698136} :answer-field/id #uuid "136e6231-d339-54ec-89cd-db326348eb00" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61ea9d23-23b8-52d0-9f63-b7e54a8e249b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698119}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698119} :answer-field/id #uuid "42f5cb7a-f946-5338-af4d-cec632603cb1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ffcee8f-b660-5909-9d6b-1706297249eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698115}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698115} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a32878-70f2-5074-b9d0-a40eb88244f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b58c8abe-2f94-54d5-96d8-ac84c9817dff" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=t^{2} - 2,\\qquad y=3 t + 3,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=\\left(-2\\right)^{2} - 2=2$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |" :question/worked-solution "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=\\left(-1\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $y=3 t + 3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-2) &=3 \\left(-2\\right) + 3 \\\\ &=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=\\left(2\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "764e1e16-b9b5-5e51-9f35-1d0ddee4c232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698124} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f1faedd-0bee-57d0-b3b8-51b2904f51bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a934d031-fb2b-58ec-9e86-a18e325d3d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698129} :answer-field/id #uuid "39314eb8-e399-5546-8673-a418f7b4eb67" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a563dad-edcc-5f5f-8fb3-7e77cbcd139d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698108}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698108} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf83c4af-598a-5a64-984f-14664cdfb9b3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f00473b1-3cdf-546b-8785-e2f69f16700e" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=- t^{2} - 2,\\qquad y=2 t - 3,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=- \\left(-2\\right)^{2} - 2=-6$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | $-3$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-1$. Substitute into $x=- t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-1) &=- \\left(-1\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $y=2 t - 3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-2) &=2 \\left(-2\\right) - 3 \\\\ &=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=- t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=- \\left(2\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-3$ | $-6$ |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20038365-556a-554d-832f-8de617ae3321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698109}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698109} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b65411e-d709-50f1-a8e3-6991f23a4f06" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b17fbbd2-22ba-59d7-b46d-a44d71fd87b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698132} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e1c7517-803a-5992-837a-97f2924d48ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73ff40ea-ec30-5b41-bc55-ff735c2859ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698123}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698123} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae672d7b-70e0-5702-b631-fbbc15772c9e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd565012-a3a9-5a51-b22a-e588daee81a8" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3 t - 1,\\qquad y=- t^{2} - 2,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-1)=3 \\left(-1\\right) - 1=-4$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-3}} | $-4$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} | $-3$ | {{field-2}} |" :question/worked-solution "The missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=- t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=- \\left(0\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $y=- t^{2} - 2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) &=- \\left(2\\right)^{2} - 2 \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=3 t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-2) &=3 \\left(-2\\right) - 1 \\\\ &=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-3$ | $-6$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01d3446f-83f3-5f5d-915a-93a112a3392f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x>-2,\\,y\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698164} {:answer/id #uuid "1a25455f-807b-5065-8c5c-7ea0a2cbbc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -2,\\,y\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698168} {:answer/id #uuid "51d41148-1b5b-5a5c-b142-a9fbb2f79a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -2,\\,y\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698178} {:answer/id #uuid "7a50f6cc-826c-5058-9d00-1263eba7aa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -2,\\,y\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698185} {:answer/id #uuid "85a9baf9-1cb1-536f-9be1-4cd505d934dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -2,\\,y\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698185} :answer-field/id #uuid "538dca6c-a148-55fc-9cdb-fa57dd3d6ae2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "17262819-bd13-5022-aa61-e611e17eb869" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t - 1,\\quad y=2 t - 1,\\quad t\\ge -1 ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=t - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine coefficient is $1$. The boundary $t=-1$ gives $x=-2$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded above, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $x\\ge -2$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=2 t - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine coefficient is $2$. The boundary $t=-1$ gives $y=-3$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded above, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $y\\ge -3$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\ge -2,\\,y\\ge -3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "117086fe-ef05-5316-a480-ea1f387be4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 4,\\,y\\ge -12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698166} {:answer/id #uuid "310a6139-2f20-5369-9255-f33101b1f002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -4,\\,y\\le -8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698174} {:answer/id #uuid "53947b6d-f5ed-5e61-966a-951fe7971a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 4,\\,y\\ge -12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698180} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6f6eb3-4e8f-5939-8373-e4da9a177976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 4,\\,y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698183} {:answer/id #uuid "df49156a-8d7d-5a5c-9360-604396a4aaee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 4,\\,y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698199}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698199} :answer-field/id #uuid "c06a009d-d21a-59ef-a074-adfe0e156e25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "32a6587f-9e92-5704-a6aa-39ec7571630f" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4 - t^{2},\\quad y=- t^{2} + 4 t - 8,\\quad t\\in(-\\infty,\\infty) ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=4 - t^{2} \\\\ &=4 - t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square takes every nonnegative value. Equality occurs at $t=0$. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $x\\le 4$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=- t^{2} + 4 t - 8 \\\\ &=- \\left(t - 2\\right)^{2} - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square takes every nonnegative value. Equality occurs at $t=2$. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $y\\le -4$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\le 4,\\,y\\le -4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d50e073-c1cd-52a2-b635-02e18958ff7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698184}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698184} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ad6dca4-1123-59f9-9a74-39990f53df1e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae80697-9ee1-5a2d-aac6-a2a36b620343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698176}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698176} :answer-field/id #uuid "23453b33-a427-520d-9940-bc0c2d3ff5ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfff7eb1-ef1b-5b07-bd86-578617bc5e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698200}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698200} :answer-field/id #uuid "92302048-697b-5c66-8fcc-fc9ca43929b7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216dfcaf-b73a-567f-8a8a-ec4643191b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698171}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698171} :answer-field/id #uuid "c32f8387-5a2f-5199-b6fc-06c3727b00ee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "aeaa24bc-4369-5201-97b7-ded344b5f202" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-\\sqrt{- t}+4,\\quad y=-2\\sqrt{3 - t},\\quad t\\le -1 ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$.\n\n$x$ {{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n\n$y$ {{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=-\\sqrt{- t}+4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radicand starts at $1$ and increases without bound along the allowed half-line. The square root is increasing, and its exterior coefficient is $-1$. The boundary $t=-1$ gives $x=3$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $x\\le 3$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=-2\\sqrt{3 - t}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radicand starts at $4$ and increases without bound along the allowed half-line. The square root is increasing, and its exterior coefficient is $-2$. The boundary $t=-1$ gives $y=-4$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $y\\le -4$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\le 3,\\,y\\le -4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c38ea5-1642-5917-bf16-4dc22eaf76fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698182} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f98f5b5-ffda-58c0-82b2-258d082d28f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c658976a-cf7c-52c6-835a-8bf06fd8eb87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698197}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698197} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e864ec2-5835-50f0-88b9-3238eb75877b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4f9039-980a-52c7-b150-91e1d35a1ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698194}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698194} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e6a6f13-eba1-54df-ac11-1d3214ccd5a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f71dc8f1-71a5-5204-bb9b-f5e84847a181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698202}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698202} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06eb7fd-57ae-588a-a9af-70a8443ef3f6" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b3fd42af-52b6-5190-bc05-87f886a099bb" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^{2} + 3,\\quad y=- 2 t - 2,\\quad t\\ge -2 ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$.\n\n$x$ {{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n\n$y$ {{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=t^{2} + 3 \\\\ &=t^{2} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vertex parameter $t=0$ is inside the domain, so its value $3$ is attained even if the parameter boundary is excluded. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded above, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $x\\ge 3$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=- 2 t - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine coefficient is $-2$. The boundary $t=-2$ gives $y=2$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $y\\le 2$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\ge 3,\\,y\\le 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c11b5f3-abc3-5979-813d-2cdfce64e78e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -6,\\,y\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698165} {:answer/id #uuid "3b832de8-1d5f-50f0-9698-bb386da2e368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -2,\\,y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698177} {:answer/id #uuid "5d551028-5a75-5c24-9883-53846da65e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -2,\\,y\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698181} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd811e9-a1cc-5b4b-98fe-f605533dec40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 2,\\,y\\le 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698186} {:answer/id #uuid "adbad31a-8750-5418-aad1-b23fadbde56c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 2,\\,y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698181} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee97b750-d5aa-5d0f-ad90-c1ece47596f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cbbf5810-ec24-5077-83b3-c6ce77d898cf" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=- 2 t - 4,\\quad y=4 - 2 t,\\quad t\\ge -1 ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=- 2 t - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine coefficient is $-2$. The boundary $t=-1$ gives $x=-2$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $x\\le -2$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=4 - 2 t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe affine coefficient is $-2$. The boundary $t=-1$ gives $y=6$ and is included. The coordinate is continuous on the domain and unbounded below, so every value on the stated side of the bound occurs. Thus $y\\le 6$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\le -2,\\,y\\le 6$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "289c39fc-e0bc-584f-890d-50f8830e1b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698218}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698218} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d62c329-d6f1-5943-92c5-5c1fd35cb85a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a926ca61-68de-581a-91c6-ea9ae885b7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698247} :answer-field/id #uuid "36f24247-97ae-5c32-b43d-b2fa5999b850" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698222} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19266755-9b43-5a85-8306-f5886ca9fb4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698211}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698211} :answer-field/id #uuid "680608f0-6553-547c-8e2a-1b025cd38d56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0abc128-d26e-51de-808e-7e52e5193b59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698258}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698258} :answer-field/id #uuid "781a8ee5-2e11-5364-b824-e33c88a22fa7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9ab8590-7cb2-5e99-9247-cdc42e135d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698253} :answer-field/id #uuid "e31d7123-9282-5508-add7-ab9b940dcbaf" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3659a41-6278-5295-abb8-8687c252f662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698246}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698246} :answer-field/id #uuid "e697811e-4a3f-5144-a05e-7398249d05d7" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "406c7ad1-7d78-5626-ac50-63adda31fea9" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\nx=-4\\cos\\theta-2,\\qquad y=5\\sin\\theta-2,\\\\\n0\\le \\theta<2\\pi,\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x\\le$ {{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}} $\\le y$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\cos\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiplying by $-4$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $-2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n4 &\\ge-4\\cos\\theta\\ge-4 \\\\\n2 &\\ge-4\\cos\\theta-2\\ge-6 \\\\\n-6 &\\le x\\le 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-6\\le x\\le 2$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\sin\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiply by $5$ and translate by $-2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-5 &\\le 5\\sin\\theta\\le 5 \\\\\n-7 &\\le 5\\sin\\theta-2\\le 3 \\\\\n-7 &\\le y\\le 3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-7\\le y\\le 3$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value."}]}
